{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Plugins"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Composing-Large-Games","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/SplittingAGameAcrossFiles","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContents","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GamePlugin","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ScoreDeclaring"],"title":"Composing Large Games"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"plugins.png","type":"image"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A content bundle (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":") splits a game’s own world across types and packages. A plugin does something else: it packages a reusable ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"system","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — spellcasting, a wall clock, combat — so a second game can import it. The seven ","type":"text"},{"code":"Gnusto*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" libraries in this repo are all built this way, and so is the ","type":"text"},{"code":"buy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"sell","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" logic you would otherwise hand-copy into every shop game.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A plugin is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"logic only","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":". It contributes the vocabulary its system needs and the rules that react to it, and owns no rooms, items, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" state; everything it touches is declared by the host game and handed to it as a parameter. A plugin that needs a room of its own is not a plugin.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"A plugin is a `GamePlugin`","anchor":"A-plugin-is-a-GamePlugin"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["extension Intent {","    #verb(\"haggle\", [\"haggle\", \"over\", .directObject])","}","","struct CommercePlugin: GamePlugin {","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] {","        .haggle","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"verbs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"actions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"timers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" all default to empty, so a plugin declares only what it needs. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"#verb","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" declarations (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":") give the plugin ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" its hosts the same typed constants — host rules key on ","type":"text"},{"code":".haggle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" exactly as the plugin’s verbs emit it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Note what ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"isn’t","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" declared here. ","type":"text"},{"code":"buy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"sell","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are engine stub verbs (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StubVerbs","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), so the words are already in every game’s vocabulary; a commerce plugin only has to supply the behavior, which it does with the rules below. ","type":"text"},{"code":"haggle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is genuinely the plugin’s own, so it needs the ","type":"text"},{"code":"#verb","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoMeleeCombat","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" splits the same way: the ","type":"text"},{"code":"attack","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" family is promoted, ","type":"text"},{"code":"stab","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"strike","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are added.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A plugin’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"timers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" splice the same way (","type":"text"},{"code":"var timers: [TimedEvent] { actors.timers }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), and parameterized timer ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"factories","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" — methods returning a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TimedEvent","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for the host’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"timers","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block — are how a plugin animates the host’s actors on the end-of-turn clock. A bare timer name the host or another bundle also declares is namespaced into the declaring bundle’s namespace at bootstrap, so prefixes are a courtesy rather than a requirement (","type":"text"},{"code":"\"actors.roam\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") — but an unambiguous name keeps its bare schedule key, which is also its save-file key.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The host splices verbs and rules","anchor":"The-host-splices-verbs-and-rules"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The host stores the plugin as a plain property and splices its vocabulary into its own ","type":"text"},{"code":"verbs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block. A plain plugin property is neither a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", nor ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so the bootstrap’s reflection walk ignores it — it never becomes an entity and never collides.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":".price","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" below is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"TraitKey<Int>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" declared once (","type":"text"},{"code":"extension TraitKey<Int> { static let price = Self(\"price\") }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") — see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomStateAndTraits","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["struct LampShop: Game {","    let commerce = CommercePlugin()","    @Global var purse = Purse(coins: 10)          \/\/ the HOST owns the wallet","    let lantern = Item { name(\"brass lantern\"); trait(.price, 5) }","","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] { commerce.verbs }    \/\/ splice the vocabulary","    \/\/ rules below","}"]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Parameterized rules over host entities","anchor":"Parameterized-rules-over-host-entities"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin’s rules need the host’s own lantern and purse — things it can’t know about in advance. So rules that touch host state are exposed as ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"parameterized methods","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" returning ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", which the host calls with its own declarations. The wallet is handed in as closures that read and adjust the host’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; they run under the live turn, so they see and mutate state exactly as an inline rule would.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["extension CommercePlugin {","    @RuleBuilder","    func purchase(","        of item: Item,","        balance: @escaping @Sendable () -> Int,","        charge:  @escaping @Sendable (Int) -> Void","    ) -> Rules {","        item.before(.buy) {","            let price = item[.price] ?? 0","            guard balance() >= price else {","                try refuse(\"You can't afford the \\(item.name); it costs \\(price) coins.\")","            }","            charge(price)","            try reply(\"You buy the \\(item.name) for \\(price) coins. You have \\(balance()) left.\")","        }","    }","}","","\/\/ in the host:","var rules: Rules {","    commerce.purchase(of: lantern,","                      balance: { purse.coins },","                      charge:  { purse.coins -= $0 })","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The protocol’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" requirement is for self-contained, world-scoped rules that need nothing from the host; anything host-specific goes through a factory method like this.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"A plugin can contribute only vocabulary","anchor":"A-plugin-can-contribute-only-vocabulary"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The rules are optional. A plugin can teach the parser a word and leave the behavior to the host, which handles the shared intent in its own ","type":"text"},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["extension Intent {","    #verb(\"appraise\", [\"appraise\", .directObject])","}","","struct Appraiser: GamePlugin {","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] {","        .appraise","    }","}","","\/\/ in the host:","var rules: Rules {","    gem.before(.appraise) {","        try reply(\"The \\(gem.name) is worth \\(gem[.price] ?? 0) coins.\")","    }","}"]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The one thing the host doesn’t splice","anchor":"The-one-thing-the-host-doesnt-splice"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GamePlugin\/statusFields","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" adds ","type":"text"},{"code":"name=value","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pairs to the play-test status footer, and it is the single member the host gets by ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"storing","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the plugin rather than by splicing it into a block of its own:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["struct Barometer: GamePlugin {","    var statusFields: [(String, String)] { [(\"glass\", \"falling\")] }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Everything else here changes what the game does, so the host opts in by hand. A status field annotates a transcript the host already asked for and changes nothing about the world — and there is no ","type":"text"},{"code":"Game","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block to splice it into — so the bootstrap reads it off the host’s stored properties, the same walk that catches an unlisted bundle. A plugin the host stores is found; one constructed inline inside a computed property is not.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The field is read inside a live turn frame that is then discarded, so it must be read-only — and it is sampled at the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"close","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" of the turn rather than after the turn’s counter advanced, so a field derived from ","type":"text"},{"code":"moves","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" names the turn it is printed under. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles#A-bundle-can-add-a-field-to-the-status-footer","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for the full contract, sampling point included, which is identical for both protocols.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Content-bearing plugins own their region","anchor":"Content-bearing-plugins-own-their-region"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A logic-only ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GamePlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" declares no world of its own — it operates entirely over entities the host passes it. A plugin that needs to ship its ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"own","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" rooms, items, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" state is a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" instead: a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" carries ","type":"text"},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"verbs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the bootstrap discovers its entities by reflection, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ContentBundles#EntityIDs-are-namespaced-by-the-bundle","overridingTitle":"namespacing","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"text":"namespacing","type":"text"}],"type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" them under the bundle so a reusable plugin can’t collide with the host. List it in the game’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"content","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The two roles compose in one type. A single struct can conform to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameContent","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" (for its auto-namespaced region and self-contained rules) ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" expose host-facing rule factories exactly like a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GamePlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" — factories are just methods returning ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Rules","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", so any type can offer them:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["extension Intent {","    #verb(\"donate\", [\"donate\", .directObject])","}","","struct ShrineContent: GameContent {","    let shrine = Location { name(\"Stone Shrine\"); description(\"…\") }   \/\/ its own room","    @Global var visits = 0                                             \/\/ its own state","","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] { .donate }","    var rules: Rules { shrine.onEnter { visits += 1; try reply(\"…\") } }  \/\/ self-contained","","    \/\/ Host-facing factory over a host item + host global — the GamePlugin pattern.","    func offering(of item: Item,","                  merit: @escaping @Sendable () -> Int,","                  credit: @escaping @Sendable (Int) -> Void) -> Rules {","        item.before(.donate) { credit(item[.value] ?? 0)","            try reply(\"Your merit rises to \\(merit()).\") }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The host lists it in ","type":"text"},{"code":"content","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (registering the namespaced region) ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" splices the factory into its own ","type":"text"},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", wiring it to host declarations:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["struct PilgrimGame: Game {","    let shrineKit = ShrineContent()","    @Global var merit = 0","    let coin = Item { name(\"brass coin\"); trait(.value, 7) }","","    var content: GameContents { shrineKit }","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] { shrineKit.verbs }","    var rules: Rules {","        shrineKit.offering(of: coin, merit: { merit }, credit: { merit += $0 })","    }","    \/\/ map: place coin in shrineKit.shrine, wire plaza ↔ shrineKit.shrine, …","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"References stay token-based across the boundary, so a host item can sit in a plugin room and a plugin rule can hook a host entity regardless of the namespace.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The first-party plugins","anchor":"The-first-party-plugins"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Seven shipped library products exercise both plugin shapes for real — each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"imports only ","type":"text"},{"code":"Gnusto","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the Zork 1 executable target is the worked","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"example that wires the first four:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Product","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Shape","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Owns","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The host passes","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoDangerousDark"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameContent"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one dark-turn counter, the grue daemon","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Text"},{"text":" + grace period at init; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"suspended"},{"text":" to make the dark harmless for a stretch (never ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stopDaemon(\"grue\")"},{"text":", which freezes the count)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoScoring"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameContent"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"award-once registers","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the award table to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(awards:)"},{"text":", treasures + the trophy case to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"treasures(_:into:)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoActors"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GamePlugin"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"nothing — position ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"is","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the actor’s placement","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"actors, room sets, candidates to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"roams"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"steals"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reaction"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoMeleeCombat"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameContent"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the combat ledger (health\/stun\/engagement by key)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"villains, weapons, prose to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"villain"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"aggression"},{"text":", and each villain’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"strikesFirst"},{"text":" odds of picking a fight nobody offered him","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoSpellcasting"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameContent"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the spell memory and the energy pool","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"spells + their ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SpellCost"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spell(_:called:cost:effect:)"},{"text":"; a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Text"},{"text":" for the system’s own refusals and the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spells"},{"text":" report","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoClock"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameContent"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the clock’s offset and pause state","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"start time, minutes per turn, alarms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"at(_:named:perform:)"},{"text":", timetables to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"schedule(_:named:_:)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoConversation"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameContent"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the facts the player has worked out, and which answers each actor has already given","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"actors + topic rows to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"topics(of:)"},{"text":" (with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"again:"},{"text":" lines for the answers that should land once), opening lines to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greeting(of:)"},{"text":", evidence to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"shows(_:to:)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Three spellings are shared across the set, so a label learned in one library holds in the next. A daemon or alarm a library declares takes its timer name as ","type":"text"},{"code":"named:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"roams(thief, named: \"thief.roams\", …)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"at(time, named: \"clock.blast\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — and the engine’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"daemon(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"fuse(_:after:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" take theirs unlabeled. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"() -> Bool","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gate is ","type":"text"},{"code":"when:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in a library as in a conditional exit or a topic row. And every library that prints a line of its own takes a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" at init — ","type":"text"},{"code":"MeleeCombat.Text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Conversation.Text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Spellcasting.Text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"DangerousDark.Text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Clock.Text","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — with the stock wording as the default, so a game re-voices the lines it cares about and leaves the rest.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The split follows one rule: a system that needs its own saved state is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" bundle (its ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s namespace automatically and travel in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"saves); a stateless toolkit is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"GamePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Plugin prose arrives as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"init and factory parameters","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" with sensible defaults — ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fixed struct, so a plugin can’t add lines to it retroactively; what it can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"do is take its lines from the host, which also keeps every player-visible","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"string in the game’s own voice.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Worked examples","anchor":"Worked-examples"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Sources\/Lighthouse\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — a small host that splices just two: ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoScoring","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (a ","type":"text"},{"code":"visit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" award and a one-off ","type":"text"},{"code":"awardOnce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", both declared in its award table so the bootstrap can check ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxScore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") and ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoActors","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (a roaming keeper). The smallest of these examples.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Sources\/Zork1\/Zork1.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the host that wires ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoActors","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoDangerousDark","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoMeleeCombat","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoScoring","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over entities declared in its own content bundles.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Sources\/Gramarye\/Gramarye.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — a small original game built entirely around ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoSpellcasting","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with one puzzle per casting paradigm.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Sources\/Fulminate\/Fulminate.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the mystery demo, built around ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoClock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": an evening on a wall clock with three alarms bracketing it. Its story and mechanics contract live in ","type":"text"},{"code":"docs\/games\/fulminate.md","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Sources\/KindlyDeep\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — a survival-and-companion host: ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoActors.follows","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a mule who trails you, is parked by a crawl he cannot fit through, and rejoins through a door, plus ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoScoring.awardOnce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on each of its five beats.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Tests\/GnustoTests\/Support\/CommerceGame.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the logic-only commerce plugin (","type":"text"},{"code":"buy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"sell","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" verbs, ","type":"text"},{"code":"purchase","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"sale","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" factories, ","type":"text"},{"code":"LampShop","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" host); ","type":"text"},{"code":"PluginTests","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" drives a buy\/sell turn end to end.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Tests\/GnustoTests\/Support\/ShrineContent.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the content-bearing ","type":"text"},{"code":"ShrineContent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin (owns a namespaced shrine region ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and"}]},{"text":" exposes an ","type":"text"},{"code":"offering","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" factory) with its ","type":"text"},{"code":"PilgrimGame","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" host; ","type":"text"},{"code":"ContentPluginTests","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" drives a donate turn across the namespace boundary and checks the namespacing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":